{
  "_about": "Resident challenges (postgame; docs/mods/resident-challenges.md). Once the game is beaten, at every midnight one recruited resident of these rows leaves its home and waits at its recruit site, stronger; won once, it goes home with its reward and nobody else goes out that day; lost, it waits all day. tools/balance.py writes `rule`, `save` and each row's species and sheet stats into MOD_CHALLENGE (tools/city_residents.py challenge_table); the story (story/mods/what-the-island-forgot) has the rest of each row: `story` checks its constant (state.py CH_<NAME> = row number), site, exit path, item and bits. Rows are numbered in the save (the challenger var and the bag: saved wide registers w10-w14, one bit a row): once released, a row is never moved or removed, only appended.",
  "rule": {
    "stats": "max-sheet-or-partner",
    "_stats": "each stat of the challenger = max(floor stat x (100 + sheetPercent) / 100, partner stat x (100 + partnerPercent) / 100), at most 9999; the floor is the species' `wild` sheet, or the row's `base` when its species has none",
    "sheetPercent": 0,
    "_sheetPercent": "the species sheet is the hard minimum: 0 or more, never negative (the loader refuses a negative value)",
    "partnerPercent": 25,
    "noItems": true,
    "noLateStep": true,
    "_noLateStep": "true: the challenge fight has none of battle-formulas.json normal's late-game step (HP and attack ramp, damage floor), on any difficulty: the challenger's stats are exactly the rule's. HARD keeps its own factors and floor.",
    "stages": "same-or-lower",
    "_stages": "same-or-lower: only residents whose stage is the partner's or lower go out, the partner's own stage first, then the next one down, each one once per cycle (a shuffle bag); any: every stage, once per cycle. Never the one of the day before."
  },
  "save": {
    "challengerVar": 15,
    "bagWreg": 10,
    "wonFlag": 783,
    "triedFlag": 784,
    "armedPstat": 239
  },
